129	Scanning Photometer Data in Zhongshan Station, Antarctica	The Meridian Scanning Photometer installed at Zhongshan Station is one of the\nPolar Research Institute of China (PRIC) and the National Institute of Polar\nResearch (NIPR) of Japan cooperative projects, which observes aurora variations\nin three wavelengths (427.8nm, 557.7nm and 630nm) along the invariant meridian;\nits scanning range extends almost from horizon to horizon. The observation was\nstarted in March 1995. However, it was interrupted during the period of July\n1995 through Feb. 1997.  The data is only valid for dark time. In other words,\nthere is no valid data during the middle of October to the beginning of March\nevery year.	dataset	\N	NASA Earthdata	C1214608750-SCIOPS	\N	\N	2026-09-20 21:43:27.777907
