160	Geology of Seymour Island, Antarctica	Currently, the data set is comprised of approximately 450\ngranulometric analyses of 70 loose grain mineralogical preparations\nfrom 30 geological sections of Seymour Island, Antarctica.  The data\nset also includes 100 microprobe heavy mineral analyses of sandstones from\nthe La Meseta Formation.  Fifty thin sections of sandstones from the Sobral,\nCross Valley, and La Meseta Formations have been prepared.	dataset	\N	NASA Earthdata	C1214610940-SCIOPS	\N	\N	2026-09-20 21:43:29.570871
